From 55669ca9569fe67530eb2242506546fc514eb1b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:04:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: stop PDR startup work before probe
 unwind

Carry this reviewed SLIMbus/BAM change into maintained Linux 6.18.
Preserve the existing LTS channel-removal/reconfigure protocol, socket
interfaces and DMA provider implementation. This stage is exact patch.

The completed eighteen-change series passes 3,221 source-bound synthetic
cases and 117 independent regression controls, with normal LeakSanitizer
and fail-fast address/undefined-behavior sanitizers. These cover
startup, child and parent ownership, QMI allocation, TX completion
lifetime, synchronous/asynchronous response ownership, DMA admission and
the retained LTS stream caller. Baselines from the appropriate
intermediate stages fail their targeted assertions. All 108 ARM, ARM64
and ARM64 RT component objects build with W=1 and nonpermissive CFI
without diagnostics; their ELF source checksums match the final
candidate.

Kernel waits, workqueues, IDR, PM, packets, DMA and device services in
the host models are synthetic. No real firmware, audio, hardware,
network, phone or installed package executes. Full current-kernel link,
physical DMA-stop/recovery and final-image acceptance remain
unqualified. Codex prepared the LTS adaptations and qualification.
Preserve original authors, dates, notices and assistance credits. Human
DCO and owner, security and subsystem review remain pending; no new
sign-off is added.

Original reviewed changelog and provenance:

The PDR lookup runs before SSR notifier registration. If the latter
fails, PDR may already have queued or started ngd_up_work. The existing
unwind removes the NGD child before releasing the PDR provider, allowing
both an in-flight callback and its startup work to outlive that child.

Release PDR and drain startup work before unregistering the child. Jump
to the workqueue cleanup afterward so the PDR handle is released once.
Keep the earlier child-registration failure unwind unchanged.

Six synthetic probe-unwind cases execute the exact parent and startup
callbacks, with queued/running work and a provider callback completing
at release. Ten ordering checks fail before this change and none fail
afterward. Devices, providers and workqueues are pthread-backed models.
Child-only unbind, master work, IRQ/DMA quiescence and physical
acceptance remain separate work.

OpenAI Codex implemented the fix, changelog and host qualification.
Human review and DCO certification are pending.

Fixes: 2a9d50e9ea40 ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: Register callbacks after creating the ngd")

Backported from commit fd5ebcf3b32e ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: stop PDR
startup work before probe unwind")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index 50eb9c0873a56..b922359c0137b 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1772,7 +1772,10 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 
 err_unregister_ngd:
+	pdr_handle_release(ctrl->pdr);
+	cancel_work_sync(&ctrl->ngd_up_work);
 	qcom_slim_ngd_unregister(ctrl);
+	goto err_destroy_mwq;
 err_pdr_release:
 	pdr_handle_release(ctrl->pdr);
 err_destroy_mwq:
-- 
2.56.0

